# CLI code standards

Run `pnpm run lint` from `packages/cli` for Oxlint, CLI-specific rules, and
Oxfmt. Run `pnpm run lint:fix` to apply safe fixes and formatting. The root
pre-commit hook uses the same tools for staged files.

- Prefer strict types and `unknown` to `any`; narrow input before use.
- Use `const`, Node `node:*` APIs, and argument arrays for child processes.
- Await promises and handle errors at the right boundary. Never use an async
  Promise executor or silently discard a failed operation.
- Keep command output in `CommandOutput` and diagnostics in the tagged logger.
- Avoid top-level browser/Node APIs that break supported runtimes.
- Keep tests isolated, with assertions in `it()`/`test()` and no disabled cases.
- Use `// oxlint-disable-next-line <rule> -- <reason>` only for an intentional
  exception. Unused suppressions fail CI; remove them when fixing the code.

The CLI-specific Oxlint rules live in `lint-rules/cli-oxlint-plugin.js`.
